Hello, my name is **Migbuild (@migbuild1911 on Discord)**, and I am the **Team Leader for the Video Team**!

Before continuing with this doc, please read the [General Onboarding Document](/guides/onboardings/general-onboarding/).

---

## What We Do

The video team is responsible for creating various videos needed for the project (promo videos, tutorials, etc.) and is also responsible for video conversion/compression (for in-game videos)

---

## Contributions

The process of assigning tasks is self-directed. You'll need to select a task from the [GitHub Project Board](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%8E%A5+video%22) from the **“Ready”** tab & assign yourself. Sometimes, team leads will ask you to do some issues as well.

Once you have finished, please share the completed video to the #video-lounge for feedback. Once we've given the OK, you can upload the files to the Video team’s folder in [Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AFeO9BUEUAk4rjtS9qVomzTrRqkwQMvz?usp=drive_link).

Make sure that you strictly follow the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing). If you want to work on an issue that isn’t on the roadmap, make sure you get approval from the team lead (migbuild1911) or the project lead (thebosst). If you want to work on an issue that IS on the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing), find the associated GitHub issue! If you can’t find it, feel free to make a new issue under the “New” tab.

All Video team members are required to read [Video Team Reference](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UrBlzv8f9bJTpV0XdWXYiLkj27uyMScQN2cweOwOlvI/edit?usp=sharing) & [Art Standards](https://docs.p3dual.com/references/art-standards/).

---

## AI Usage Policy

- There will be **NO** usage of Generative AI within the Video Team. Anyone found to be using it for the project will be kicked from the team, and have their contributions removed.

---

## Tools & Setup

Primary Video NLE: DaVinci Resolve / Adobe Premiere\
Graphics & Compositing: Adobe After Effects / Adobe Photoshop / Adobe Illustrator

Audio Editing: DaVinci Fairlight / Adobe Audition / Ableton Live/ REAPER/ Fl Studio\
\
Container & Codec: MP4 / H.264

- Frame Rate: [24fps / 30fps / 60fps] *(Stick to one standard across the project)*
- Target Bitrate:
  - 1080p (16:9): 15–20 Mbps
  - 1080p Vertical (9:16): 10–12 Mbps
  - 4K: 45–60 Mbps

